# Authentication — the decisions to make before writing it

Authentication is where an app leaks its architecture. Five choices, each with a cost you pay later,
and none of them are ours to make for you. Record each with `/decide` so it is not re-argued.

## 1. Where the session lives

| Option | Cost |
|---|---|
| **A `SessionProviding` protocol in `Core`, one actor implementing it** *(recommended)* | Every consumer injects it; nothing reaches for a global. Slightly more wiring at the root |
| A singleton `SessionManager.shared` | Free to write, impossible to test — and it violates CLAUDE.md §2.6, so the rule has to go first |

## 2. Where the token is stored

Keychain, always — through a `SecretStoring` protocol so tests never touch the real one
(`StorageKit`). `UserDefaults` for a token is a finding, not an option. Decide only *what* is stored:
refresh token alone, or the access token too.

## 3. Who refreshes, and when

| Option | Cost |
|---|---|
| **A `TokenRefreshing` middleware inside the network layer** *(recommended)* | One place retries a 401, queues concurrent callers, and no feature knows tokens exist |
| Each feature checks expiry before its call | Every new screen re-implements it, and one that forgets ships a random logout |

Concurrency matters here: two screens hitting a 401 at once must produce **one** refresh, not two.
That is a single in-flight task the middleware owns.

## 4. What the app shows while it does not know yet

Cold launch has a third state that is neither signed-in nor signed-out: *checking*. Model it — an
`AuthState` of `.unknown | .signedOut | .signedIn(Session)` — or the first frame flashes the wrong
screen on every launch.

## 5. What signing out actually clears

Token, cached user, in-memory caches, on-disk caches, pending uploads, push registration. Write the
list here **before** implementing, because the bug is always the one thing nobody listed.

---

**Then delete this file.** It is a decision aid, not documentation; once the decisions are recorded
in `docs/DECISIONS.md` and the code exists, this file only goes stale.
